# Capital.com Execution Safety

- Never remove disabled-by-default behavior or weaken `CAPITAL_EXECUTION_DEMO_ONLY=1`.
- Never use real credentials or call a live broker in verification.
- Preserve direction, status, confidence, risk, expiry, price freshness/deviation, Control Unit, account-selection, position-limit, and idempotency checks.
- Preserve forced account selection, account validation, and bounded 401 re-authentication.
- Never log CST, X-SECURITY-TOKEN, passwords, API keys, or full sensitive broker responses.
- Mock Capital.com in tests; execution changes require focused execution and Control Unit tests.
